      },
      "message": "feat(mcp): hole patterns from numbers for Drill, Bore and Thread\n\nAdd camcraft_geometry::hole_pattern: a point list, a line, a grid and a\nfull or partial bolt-hole circle give hole centres by plain\ntrigonometry. Bad numbers are refused by the field name.\n\nAdd the MCP tool add_hole_pattern. It makes a Drill, Bore or Thread\noperation on the stock with the pattern's holes, with no 3D model. The\nholes start at the stock top unless \"top\" is given. Model-referenced\nheights measure from the stock, so a stock-only setup generates. An\noptional spot drill on the same holes comes first. The two operations\nare one undo step. A refusal changes nothing.\n\nFixes #3195\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
